From 58c59043e60b636e4cbb1961e25d45a2923f0f10 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Hades <15710513+hadesdevls@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 20 Oct 2026 21:53:07 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] tools/dvbridge: the gamut table of the mapping to a display
 at 96x64x512

The mapping of a reconstructed picture to a display (to an SDR output, and
the projector mode) maps its colours into the display's gamut with
libplacebo's perceptual gamut mapping, read by the GPU from a table of
48x32x256 entries (intensity, chroma, hue) with linear interpolation. Where
the mapping folds a colour onto the edge of the target's gamut, a component
there is 0; an interpolated entry lands inside the gamut instead, and that
component comes out lit. Near black the EOTF is steep, so in codes of the
signal it is large: up to 521 of 4095 in a profile 5 chart mapped to SDR,
the most that remained against the double-precision reference once the PQ
EOTF of the reconstruction was exact (libplacebo-9942).

Measured on the software OpenGL ES (zink on lavapipe, libplacebo with
libplacebo-9942), against libplacebo's mapping computed on the processor
with the exact gamut mapping (no table), at four sizes. Delta E ITP (ITU-R
BT.2124), 99.9 % and largest, the profile 5 chart:

  table          SDR          projector (150 cd/m2, DCI-P3)
  48x32x256      1.27  2.22   1.71  2.42
  48x64x256      0.62  1.43   0.99  1.80
  96x64x512      0.52  1.10   0.78  1.19
  192x128x1024   0.34  0.72   0.41  0.94

and in two pictures of the FEL test stream the projector's picture had
17.7 % and 19.6 % of its pixels more than 1 away; now 0.03 % and 0.04 %.
In 12-bit codes the largest difference falls from 521 to 390 (SDR) and
from 208 to 154 (projector), always in a component that should be 0.

96x64x512 is used: the error keeps falling with the table, and the next
size (192 MB, 4.7 s to make on one core) costs too much. This one is 24 MB
instead of 3, is made once for a video when the first picture is mapped
(0.6 s instead of 0.08 s on one core of the build machine; libplacebo
spreads the work over the cores there are: 47 ms instead of 8 with 32), and
a picture costs as much to draw: 42 ms instead of 41 for 3840x2160 on the
software renderer. A picture that is not mapped is drawn as before, to the
bit; the render test of the bridge on the FEL test stream changes only in
the projector's pictures, by 1 code of 1023 at most in its patches.
---
 tools/dvbridge/dvbridge_render.c | 12 ++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 12 insertions(+)

diff --git a/tools/dvbridge/dvbridge_render.c b/tools/dvbridge/dvbridge_render.c
index 1a0dbb7..7073d2d 100644
--- a/tools/dvbridge/dvbridge_render.c
+++ b/tools/dvbridge/dvbridge_render.c
@@ -1165,6 +1165,18 @@ static void map_to_display(const struct dvbridge_hdr10_mapping *m, struct pl_col
     params->metadata = PL_HDR_METADATA_ANY;
     params->inverse_tone_mapping = false;
     params->gamut_expansion = false;
+    /* Hades: the table of the gamut mapping at twice libplacebo's resolution in each dimension
+     * (96x64x512 entries of intensity, chroma and hue instead of 48x32x256). The GPU reads it with
+     * linear interpolation, and where the mapping folds a colour onto the edge of the target's gamut
+     * (a component at 0) an interpolated entry lands inside it: the dark component comes out lit,
+     * and the steep EOTF near black shows it. Against libplacebo's mapping computed exactly, a
+     * profile 5 chart mapped to SDR differed by at most 2.2 Delta E ITP (99.9 %: 1.3); now 1.1
+     * (0.5). The table is 24 MB instead of 3, is made once for a video (on one core of the build
+     * machine, 0.6 s instead of 0.08 s; its work is spread over the cores there is), and a picture
+     * costs as much to draw as with the smaller one. */
+    params->lut3d_size[0] = 96;
+    params->lut3d_size[1] = 64;
+    params->lut3d_size[2] = 512;
 }
 
 /* Hades: a texture of the picture for output as HDR10, of that size (made again when it is of another) */
